# fixedbugs, defect 559, lane b18-ffi, 2026-10-10 (panel 202's C0; the
# critic's `fpwide`).
#
# `fill_wide(@x: i32)` over `void fill_wide(long long *x)`, so C writes eight
# bytes into a four-byte local, beside a module whose header cannot share a
# unit with this one's. Until 2026-10-10 the pointee check could not read the
# program's headers together and passed: this built at exit 0, and the
# binary stopped at exit 134 when C reached past the local, advising a
# `counted_by` lend where the repair is `i64`. It is refused at the build
# now, as the same binding is without the other module.
use fixedbugs559/long_twice

extern "fixedbugs-559-int.h"
    function twice(x: i32) -> i32
    function fill_wide(@x: i32)  #~ ffi_parameter_type

function main()
    y: i32 @ 0
    z: i32 @ 7
    fill_wide(@y)
    print(long_twice.doubled(x: 3))
    print(y + z + twice(x: 4))
